1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,788
Your car breaks down,

2
00:00:01,688 --> 00:00:03,965
and suddenly you need four hundred dollars

3
00:00:03,865 --> 00:00:04,743
you don't have.

4
00:00:05,023 --> 00:00:06,835
More than a third of American adults

5
00:00:06,735 --> 00:00:08,262
couldn't cover that with cash.

6
00:00:08,542 --> 00:00:10,847
Here's how to build an emergency fund,

7
00:00:10,747 --> 00:00:12,298
even on a small paycheck.

8
00:00:13,098 --> 00:00:16,002
Without savings, every surprise turns into debt.

9
00:00:16,282 --> 00:00:18,030
A flat tire or a doctor visit

10
00:00:17,930 --> 00:00:19,905
goes straight onto a credit card,

11
00:00:19,805 --> 00:00:22,575
and the interest makes next month even tighter.

12
00:00:22,855 --> 00:00:25,115
An emergency fund breaks that cycle.

13
00:00:25,015 --> 00:00:27,395
It's the money that stands between you

14
00:00:27,295 --> 00:00:28,176
and new debt.

15
00:00:28,976 --> 00:00:30,667
You may have heard you need three

16
00:00:30,567 --> 00:00:32,210
to six months of expenses saved.

17
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:34,257
That's a great long term goal,

18
00:00:34,157 --> 00:00:36,646
but on a low income it can feel impossible.

19
00:00:36,926 --> 00:00:39,041
So start smaller. Your first goal is

20
00:00:38,941 --> 00:00:40,217
five hundred dollars.

21
00:00:40,497 --> 00:00:42,559
That alone covers a lot of common

22
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:44,521
surprises, like a car repair or a

23
00:00:44,421 --> 00:00:45,532
new phone screen.

24
00:00:45,812 --> 00:00:46,750
Once you hit it,

25
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:48,793
you can raise the goal to one thousand.

26
00:00:49,593 --> 00:00:52,367
Next, find a little money that's already slipping away.

27
00:00:52,647 --> 00:00:54,863
Look for subscriptions and apps you forgot

28
00:00:54,763 --> 00:00:55,769
you're paying for.

29
00:00:56,049 --> 00:00:57,345
Check for bank fees,

30
00:00:57,245 --> 00:00:59,676
like overdraft or monthly account fees.

31
00:00:59,576 --> 00:01:02,007
Many banks offer accounts without them.

32
00:01:02,287 --> 00:01:04,415
And notice the small daily extras,

33
00:01:04,315 --> 00:01:06,145
like snacks or delivery fees.

34
00:01:06,425 --> 00:01:08,353
Even sixty dollars a month adds up

35
00:01:08,253 --> 00:01:10,665
to seven hundred and twenty dollars a year.

36
00:01:11,465 --> 00:01:13,216
Now pick an amount you can save

37
00:01:13,116 --> 00:01:15,294
every single week, no matter how small.

38
00:01:15,574 --> 00:01:17,797
Ten dollars a week becomes five hundred

39
00:01:17,697 --> 00:01:19,377
and twenty dollars in a year.

40
00:01:19,657 --> 00:01:22,558
Twenty five dollars a week becomes thirteen hundred.

41
00:01:22,838 --> 00:01:25,775
And fifty dollars a week becomes twenty six hundred.

42
00:01:26,055 --> 00:01:28,414
The amount matters less than the habit.

43
00:01:28,314 --> 00:01:30,499
Consistency is what builds the fund.

44
00:01:31,299 --> 00:01:33,473
The easiest way to stay consistent is

45
00:01:33,373 --> 00:01:35,042
to take willpower out of it.

46
00:01:35,322 --> 00:01:37,650
Set up an automatic transfer to your

47
00:01:37,550 --> 00:01:39,197
emergency fund on payday.

48
00:01:39,477 --> 00:01:41,766
Many banks and credit unions let you

49
00:01:41,666 --> 00:01:43,346
split your direct deposit,

50
00:01:43,246 --> 00:01:46,751
so part of each paycheck lands in savings automatically.

51
00:01:47,031 --> 00:01:48,461
Then your bills get paid,

52
00:01:48,361 --> 00:01:50,003
and the rest is for spending.

53
00:01:50,283 --> 00:01:52,171
Money you never see in your checking

54
00:01:52,071 --> 00:01:54,456
account is money you won't accidentally spend.

55
00:01:55,256 --> 00:01:56,833
Where you keep the money matters too.

56
00:01:57,113 --> 00:01:59,080
If it sits in your checking account,

57
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:00,273
it's too easy to spend.

58
00:02:00,553 --> 00:02:02,894
Keep it in a separate savings account,

59
00:02:02,794 --> 00:02:04,604
ideally a high yield one at a

60
00:02:04,504 --> 00:02:06,903
federally insured bank or credit union.

61
00:02:07,183 --> 00:02:09,476
Avoid investing your emergency fund.

62
00:02:09,376 --> 00:02:10,755
It needs to be there,

63
00:02:10,655 --> 00:02:13,070
at full value, the moment you need it.

64
00:02:13,870 --> 00:02:15,230
Want to get there faster?

65
00:02:15,130 --> 00:02:17,752
Use money that isn't part of your normal paycheck.

66
00:02:18,032 --> 00:02:19,864
A tax refund, if you get one,

67
00:02:19,764 --> 00:02:22,432
can fill your starter fund in a single day.

68
00:02:22,712 --> 00:02:24,233
A few hours of side work,

69
00:02:24,133 --> 00:02:26,279
or selling things you no longer use,

70
00:02:26,179 --> 00:02:27,359
can add up quickly.

71
00:02:27,639 --> 00:02:29,984
Even cash gifts can go straight into the fund.

72
00:02:30,264 --> 00:02:31,919
Try sending at least half of any

73
00:02:31,819 --> 00:02:32,939
surprise money there.

74
00:02:33,739 --> 00:02:35,986
Decide ahead of time what counts as

75
00:02:35,886 --> 00:02:37,029
a real emergency.

76
00:02:37,309 --> 00:02:39,347
A car repair you need for work,

77
00:02:39,247 --> 00:02:41,347
a medical bill, or a sudden drop

78
00:02:41,247 --> 00:02:42,284
in income? Yes.

79
00:02:42,564 --> 00:02:44,078
A great sale, a concert,

80
00:02:43,978 --> 00:02:45,137
or a holiday trip?

81
00:02:45,037 --> 00:02:47,316
Those deserve their own savings goal.

82
00:02:47,596 --> 00:02:49,133
And if you do use the fund,

83
00:02:49,033 --> 00:02:50,943
that's okay. That's what it's for.

84
00:02:50,843 --> 00:02:52,806
Just start refilling it right away.

85
00:02:53,606 --> 00:02:55,043
Here's the full roadmap,

86
00:02:54,943 --> 00:02:56,157
one stage at a time.

87
00:02:56,437 --> 00:02:58,042
First, five hundred dollars.

88
00:02:57,942 --> 00:02:59,386
That's your starter fund.

89
00:02:59,666 --> 00:03:01,187
Then, one thousand dollars,

90
00:03:01,087 --> 00:03:02,291
for a bigger cushion.

91
00:03:02,571 --> 00:03:05,266
Next, three months of essential expenses,

92
00:03:05,166 --> 00:03:08,241
like rent, food, utilities, and transportation.

93
00:03:08,521 --> 00:03:10,167
And over time, if you can,

94
00:03:10,067 --> 00:03:12,248
six months. Every stage makes you a

95
00:03:12,148 --> 00:03:13,734
little safer than before.

96
00:03:14,534 --> 00:03:15,480
Let's recap.

97
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:16,832
Start with a small,

98
00:03:16,732 --> 00:03:18,622
clear goal of five hundred dollars.

99
00:03:18,902 --> 00:03:22,122
Find hidden money in fees and forgotten subscriptions.

100
00:03:22,402 --> 00:03:24,123
Save a fixed amount every week.

101
00:03:24,403 --> 00:03:26,102
Automate the transfer on payday.

102
00:03:26,382 --> 00:03:27,841
And keep it in a separate,

103
00:03:27,741 --> 00:03:29,096
insured savings account.

104
00:03:29,896 --> 00:03:31,582
You don't need a big income to

105
00:03:31,482 --> 00:03:32,587
build a safety net.

106
00:03:32,487 --> 00:03:33,803
You just need to start,

107
00:03:33,703 --> 00:03:34,596
and keep going.

108
00:03:34,876 --> 00:03:36,825
If this helped, like the video and

109
00:03:36,725 --> 00:03:38,891
subscribe for more simple ways to feel

110
00:03:38,791 --> 00:03:39,924
calmer about money.

111
00:03:40,204 --> 00:03:41,568
Tell me in the comments:

112
00:03:41,468 --> 00:03:43,465
how much is your first savings goal?

113
00:03:43,365 --> 00:03:44,729
See you in the next one.
